{"title":"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Symmetry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Symmetry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Symmetry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Symmetry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Symmetry_with_Generalization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Symmetry with Generalization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Symmetry_with_Generalization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Symmetry with Generalization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Prime_Factorization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Prime Factorization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Observation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Observation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Brute_force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Brute force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40c7b33cb1d2dfd428e0b5006f98cbcc33d12a80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(31)(30)(29)(28)+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"179\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Symmetry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Symmetry)\">Solution 1 (Symmetry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Symmetry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the four numbers to multiply are symmetric with the center at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d2e532c6a286ae70230e73e30352be0901da33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29.5$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />. \nMultiply the symmetric pairs to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eafc7b705ff104d234a00465a9d1f04dbc5e4bf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31\\cdot 28=868$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d343d3f4f0798b7d1a7cccc87bd2dbdc3d759807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\cdot 29=870$\" width=\"100\" height=\"12\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c2ff98fa60ac7c1cb9b32e863ce480018fe0ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{868\\cdot 870 + 1} = \\sqrt{(869-1)(869+1) + 1} = \\sqrt{869^2 - 1^2 + 1} = \\sqrt{869^2} = \\boxed{869}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"614\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Symmetry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Symmetry)\">Solution 2 (Symmetry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Symmetry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b1abe2e211a86e4114ae6042c9f16661332a9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+1)^2 = a \\cdot (a+2) +1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"19\" />. Then we can notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e8e26d72d3987979af6582fb1d9f26a585bc305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\cdot 29 =870$\" width=\"100\" height=\"12\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/8/a883ff5bc5fef14195cae4bd17a401c74dce41e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 \\cdot 28 = 868$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c90971a1eb42e89b640f48889b201ea62614f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(31)(30)(29)(28) +1} = \\sqrt{(870)(868) +1} = \\sqrt{(868 +1)^2} = \\boxed{869}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"520\" height=\"32\" />. This is because we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/7/7c7f92d5b10d0ca62fb127d7d89a14ef7ddf5177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=868$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> as per the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b1abe2e211a86e4114ae6042c9f16661332a9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+1)^2 = a \\cdot (a+2) +1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>~qwertysri987\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Symmetry_with_Generalization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Symmetry_with_Generalization)\">Solution 3 (Symmetry with Generalization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Symmetry with Generalization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>More generally, we can prove that one more than the product of four consecutive integers must be a perfect square:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb666a2951c1d5983e0fe27c2dd6625b2754cdf7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (a+3)(a+2)(a+1)(a)+1 &amp;= [(a+3)(a)][(a+2)(a+1)]+1 \\\\ &amp;= [a^2+3a][a^2+3a+2]+1 \\\\ &amp;= [a^2+3a]^2+2[a^2+3a]+1 \\\\ &amp;= [a^2+3a+1]^2. \\end{align*}\" width=\"482\" height=\"101\" />\nAt <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c22180f2039a7deaf26262baa6e900bd3454f0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=28,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14fddff64c9860ff49613b62f5bcffe53acecf7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{(a+3)(a+2)(a+1)(a)+1}=a^2+3a+1=\\boxed{869}.\\]\" width=\"416\" height=\"32\" />\n~Novus677 ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Symmetry_with_Generalization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Symmetry_with_Generalization)\">Solution 4 (Symmetry with Generalization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Symmetry with Generalization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to Solution 1 above, call the consecutive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b39349e34bc3adedbb2fcea700cb27251bf6f546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(n-\\frac{3}{2}\\right), \\left(n-\\frac{1}{2}\\right), \\left(n+\\frac{1}{2}\\right), \\left(n+\\frac{3}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"319\" height=\"43\" /> to make use of symmetry.  Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> itself is not an integer - in this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3da174b43f66261e83a6b5b6a316ef76048e4853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 29.5$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />.  The expression becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa3d9c6fb7d878d9632d0aa70b2bd3017fb6cd9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\left(n-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\left(n + \\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\left(n - \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(n + \\frac{1}{2}\\right) + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"349\" height=\"56\" />.  Distributing each pair of difference of squares first, and then distributing the two resulting quadratics and adding the constant, gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c17dcc13b9ce15aaf35bffaad883f4c76669bbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{n^4 - \\frac{5}{2}n^2 + \\frac{25}{16}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"134\" height=\"43\" />.  The inside is a perfect square trinomial, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba021dc601e57337cbb802fad8e5f342ab29cbe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 = 4ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />.  It's equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ac0ac1542d588edce65699ed9061613e730492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\left(n^2 - \\frac{5}{4}\\right)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"105\" height=\"53\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b650ac7350262636c41ff6d2680259b4857ade4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 - \\frac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" />.  You can plug in the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> from there, or further simplify to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64eccf35f8178c35be0b602c165989e37fce5a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(n - \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(n + \\frac{1}{2}\\right) - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"181\" height=\"45\" />, which is easier to compute.  Either way, plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb8a0931ce39666b0381cb0f40ca2c5adec11f5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=29.5$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f4865d4d0080dd011e5e6b6c1be2f45c7bc77a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{869}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Prime_Factorization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Prime_Factorization)\">Solution 5 (Prime Factorization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Prime Factorization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace798d9422846a88a37b044712295ebaac92dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(31)(30)(29)(28)+1=755161.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"246\" height=\"20\" /> Since the alternating sum of the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ca33a5c979c5d5fa647bf677818ffe6f9c6f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7-5+5-1+6-1=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"207\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f480123fdee29c93742d132dcdab8439a72e45d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb69cf853f4f35dc2b236fb0bccc5efcfb5822d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$755161$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/7/4e76ce9da0f428536412a4f539b127c608760686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>We evaluate the original expression by prime factorization:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b3458b780bdefce5d1e794248782411375d5a4b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sqrt{(31)(30)(29)(28)+1}&amp;=\\sqrt{755161} \\\\ &amp;=\\sqrt{11\\cdot68651} \\\\ &amp;=\\sqrt{11^2\\cdot6241} \\\\ &amp;=\\sqrt{11^2\\cdot79^2} \\\\ &amp;=11\\cdot79 \\\\ &amp;=\\boxed{869}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"293\" height=\"178\" />\n~Vrjmath ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Observation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Observation)\">Solution 6 (Observation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Observation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The last digit under the radical is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the square root must either end in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b3e0c19a1d7ac3e6368237f92971c8fa22af30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2  = 1\\pmod {10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"19\" /> means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f424f1753ba66a66c48a233c5afe322d41467a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />.  Additionally, the number must be near <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/caeda4001c399e755c8fe6f52535ebfdb75fb117.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29 \\cdot 30 = 870$\" width=\"100\" height=\"12\" />, narrowing the reasonable choices to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72568c25ded86a7ed54e15086a82c73b049961f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$869$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c77f875af33e01a4074b1b24e82be3a804d0d1b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$871$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Continuing the logic, the next-to-last digit under the radical is the same as the last digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/8/778031ce068bd15dd1ffea5c51a60470a7775646.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28 \\cdot 29 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"102\" height=\"13\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Quick computation shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/825c8e2fd5b23366649af23c3e9d9ba333aee6b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$869^2$\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/7509da66617eeb522aafd314774074756d87fe10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$871^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba6cdde56f366d628a7a35826f98523dbe58bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.  Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f4865d4d0080dd011e5e6b6c1be2f45c7bc77a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{869}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Brute_force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Brute_force)\">Solution 7 (Brute force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Brute force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93c0573b8c27f40b08c93c36e8ab5297d59fb7ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 \\times 30 \\times 29 \\times 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/3480cb339bc7185a8d3d17397df4e2112d2284d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$755160$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b7bc47257975ed7b7f482e973f93243e8f84b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$755160 + 1=755161$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e5bf87325c6bd49370b146832ad0d378da9341e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{755161}=869$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"21\" />. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f4865d4d0080dd011e5e6b6c1be2f45c7bc77a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{869}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shunyipanda&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Shunyipanda (page does not exist)\">shunyipanda</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME\" title=\"1989 AIME\">1989 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems